{"id": 54, "ts": 1781729557.450127, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I agree with the panel\u2019s shift toward Candidate\u202fC as the provisional choice. The recent confirmations that neither Anna nor Sofia have any observations on C\u2019s numeric\u2011detail accuracy highlight a gap, but that gap is also present for Candidate\u202fB (who has a known weak memory for numbers) and for Candidate\u202fD (no data on numeric handling). In contrast, C\u2019s documented 100\u202f% reliability, calmness in crisis, quick correct decisions, and strong technical competence directly satisfy the core safety criteria of operational reliability, stress resilience, decision quality, and technical/cognitive ability. The communication and education concerns, while important, are less immediately safety\u2011critical than the proven numeric\u2011memory weakness of B and the complete lack of decision\u2011quality evidence for B. Therefore, I maintain Candidate\u202fC as my current recommendation."}
